<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`verificationCode`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`VerificationCode`" pulumi-lang-go="`verificationCode`" pulumi-lang-python="`verification_code`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`verificationCode`" pulumi-lang-java="`verificationCode`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`verification_code`">`verificationCode`</span> or <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`magicLink`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`MagicLink`" pulumi-lang-go="`magicLink`" pulumi-lang-python="`magic_link`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`magicLink`" pulumi-lang-java="`magicLink`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`magic_link`">`magicLink`</span>). Atlas ships a default subject and body for
each system email; this resource overrides the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`subject`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Subject`" pulumi-lang-go="`subject`" pulumi-lang-python="`subject`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`subject`" pulumi-lang-java="`subject`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`subject`">`subject`</span> and/or plain-text
