## #<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" atlas.WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-dotnet=" atlas.WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-go=" WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-python=" WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-yaml=" atlas.WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-java=" atlas.WebhookEndpoint
" pulumi-lang-hcl=" atlas_webhook_endpoint
"> atlas.WebhookEndpoint
</span>
A webhook endpoint that receives signed Atlas events. The signing secret
(`whsec_...`) is stored (sensitive) in state: it is returned on create, and on
import it is read back from Atlas. Changing <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`url`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Url`" pulumi-lang-go="`url`" pulumi-lang-python="`url`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`url`" pulumi-lang-java="`url`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`url`">`url`</span>, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`enabledEvents`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`EnabledEvents`" pulumi-lang-go="`enabledEvents`" pulumi-lang-python="`enabled_events`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`enabledEvents`" pulumi-lang-java="`enabledEvents`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`enabled_events`">`enabledEvents`</span> or <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`active`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Active`" pulumi-lang-go="`active`" pulumi-lang-python="`active`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`active`" pulumi-lang-java="`active`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`active`">`active`</span>
updates the endpoint **in place** and **preserves the signing secret**, so event
deliveries keep verifying. Change <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`rotateSecretTrigger`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`RotateSecretTrigger`" pulumi-lang-go="`rotateSecretTrigger`" pulumi-lang-python="`rotate_secret_trigger`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`rotateSecretTrigger`" pulumi-lang-java="`rotateSecretTrigger`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`rotate_secret_trigger`">`rotateSecretTrigger`</span> to rotate the secret
in place.

Atlas switches an endpoint off after repeated delivery failures. It then stays
in state with `active = false` (and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`failingSince`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`FailingSince`" pulumi-lang-go="`failingSince`" pulumi-lang-python="`failing_since`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`failingSince`" pulumi-lang-java="`failingSince`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`failing_since`">`failingSince`</span> / <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`disabledAt`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DisabledAt`" pulumi-lang-go="`disabledAt`" pulumi-lang-python="`disabled_at`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`disabledAt`" pulumi-lang-java="`disabledAt`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`disabled_at`">`disabledAt`</span> set); set
`active = true` to switch it back on.

Backend API (BAPI): `POST /v1/webhook_endpoints` (create),
`GET /v1/webhook_endpoints` (list — the read filters this list by id, since there
is no get-by-id route), `PATCH /v1/webhook_endpoints/:id` (in-place update — does
not rotate the secret), `POST /v1/webhook_endpoints/:id/rotate_secret`
(rotation), `POST /v1/webhook_endpoints/:id/reveal_secret` (import),
`DELETE /v1/webhook_endpoints/:id` (delete).

